{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggL59pe9PTS395bgwj7A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in `money.py`, and `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, which sums to 100.\n\n**The change:** `split_cents` used `total // people` and multiplied it out, so the remainder was dropped. It now uses `divmod` and gives one extra grosz to the first `remainder` people:\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1] * remainder + [share] * (people - remainder)\n```\n\n**Verification:** I ran a quick script on a few inputs and asserted that each result sums to the total and has the right length. That passed for `(100,3)`, `(100,1)`, `(0,4)`, `(7,7)`, `(10,4)`, `(-100,3)` and `(1,5)`. This is an ad-hoc check, not a test suite. I did not run the project's existing tests, since I didn't find any.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- The extra grosze go to the first shares, not randomly. Your tech lead may prefer a different rule for who pays the extra; this one is deterministic.\n- The `people < 1` check is unchanged.\n- I have not committed. The change is uncommitted in the working tree, so it's easy to review or revert before deploy.\n\nBefore this ships, check whether any existing caller relied on the old (lossy) behaviour, and make sure someone has a test for the remainder case ready for next sprint."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":595,"cache_read_input_tokens":19954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":595},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d53e30f1-454d-43aa-b7c5-26064cf268b8","uuid":"be0fbbc8-928c-4a90-bd84-da80a6e8c450","timestamp":"2026-11-03T16:43:11.866Z","req